  "notes": [
    "Manually reviewed all seven eligible production TypeScript files, including api.ts and provider-policy-api.ts local barrels, plus package.json and openclaw.plugin.json. All 19 files under extensions/vllm are partitioned into reviewed/excluded records, including the CLAUDE.md symlink.",
    "Every local production import/reexport stays within extensions/vllm; there is no additional plugin-owned/shared shipped source outside this root. The four .test.ts files have no production importers. No installed dependency or SDK implementation graph was recursively audited.",
    "The package openclaw.extensions entry points to index.ts. There is no metadata exception requiring generated/build output. Public SDK module specifiers and exported names were checked against package exports and the corresponding SDK facades.",
    "defineSelfHostedOpenAICompatibleProvider is an imported SDK factory called by index.ts. Registration performed inside that factory is outside this plugin source boundary; provider overrides are not literal api.on/registerHook registrations and do not yield API-member or hook findings.",
    "ProviderWrapStreamFnContext, ProviderNormalizeResolvedModelContext, ProviderDefaultThinkingPolicyContext, Model and StreamFn are provider/LLM data and callable contracts, not OpenClawPluginApi or PluginRuntime handles. Their fields, indexed accesses, Pick projection, and stream callbacks do not establish API/runtime-member provenance.",
    "SDK helper return values such as the reasoning object, payload record, Qwen kwargs and thinking profile remain ordinary returned values; accesses to their fields do not create API/runtime members. Local wrapper functions and their barrel exports preserve plugin-local ownership rather than becoming reexports of SDK helpers.",
    "All explicit imported types are retained as source dependencies with type-reference evidence. The llm module is mixed because its declaration contains resolveOpenAIRequestReasoning as a value import and Model as an inline type import; the two export identities retain separate runtime/type classifications.",
